    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_029cbe45",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: stop_illegal_immigrants_meme; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man holding a firearm next to an American flag, with text that reads 'stop illegal immigrants' and 'they're taking the land we stole.' This juxtaposition uses violent imagery and nationalist rhetoric to dehumanize and demonize immigrants, framing them as thieves and threats to American identity. The meme promotes xenophobic and racist ideologies by suggesting immigrants are stealing land and resources, which is a harmful and hateful stereotype. It aligns with anti-immigrant tropes that portray immigrants as economic and cultural threats, and it implicitly supports the idea that immigrants are undeserving of the land or resources, which can incite hostility and discrimination against immigrant communities. The overall intent is to incite fear and hatred toward immigrants, making it a hateful meme.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_7acef8ea"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
